# Web Performance (Frontend)

## Purpose

Prevent common frontend performance regressions without premature micro-optimization.

## Core Web Vitals Targets (guideline)

| Metric | Target |
|--------|--------|
| LCP | < 2.5s |
| INP | < 200ms |
| CLS | < 0.1 |

## Bundles

- Dynamic import heavy routes and modals (`React.lazy`, Next.js dynamic).
- Analyze bundle when adding large dependencies (charts, editors).
- Tree-shake: import named exports, not entire libraries.

## Rendering (React)

- `useMemo` / `useCallback` only when profiling shows benefit or referential stability required.
- Virtualize lists with 100+ items (react-window, TanStack Virtual).
- Avoid anonymous inline functions as props to memoized children when it causes rerenders.

## Images & Assets

- Use framework image optimization (next/image, responsive srcset).
- Lazy-load below-fold media; specify width/height to prevent CLS.
- Prefer modern formats (WebP, AVIF) when pipeline supports.

## Data

- Paginate or infinite-scroll large lists — never render 10k DOM nodes.
- Prefetch on hover/intent for critical navigation when using TanStack Query / router.

## Network

- Debounce search inputs; cancel in-flight requests on unmount (AbortController).
- Cache static assets with appropriate headers (framework defaults).

## When Flagging to User

If a solution adds heavy client work (large JSON parse, sync crypto), mention trade-off and lighter alternative.